{
  "name": "grasshopper",
  "_about": "A grasshopper -- the common field grasshopper (Chorthippus brunneus), 2 cm long: a big blunt head with a vertical face, large eyes and short thread antennae; a saddle-shaped pronotum with pale keels down its sides; leathery forewings (tegmina) lying along the abdomen nearly to its tip, the clear hind wings folded away under them; two small pairs of walking legs and the great jumping hind legs -- the femur long and thick, the knee dark, the spined tibia folded up under it. Coats: green, brown, purple-flushed. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/winged/others.py on insectlib.py + wlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait, antennae that wave; the wings at rest as the animal holds them, beating in the variant \"flying\").",
